      "blocks": {
        "content_1": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What snoring is",
            "level": "h2",
            "anchor": "snoring"
          }
        },
        "content_2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Snoring is the sound made when you breathe during sleep and the airway narrows.</p><p>Snoring can affect the sleep of the person who snores and the person who shares the bed.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_3": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Snoring isn't always the same",
            "level": "h2",
            "anchor": "causes"
          }
        },
        "content_4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Snoring doesn't always have the same cause. That's why there is no single solution for everyone.</p><p><strong>Snoring and sleep apnea are not the same thing.</strong> Some signs need to be checked by a healthcare provider. We list them on <a href=\"/pages/use-and-safety#when-to-talk-to-a-provider\">Use &amp; safety</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_5": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What a mandibular advancement device is",
            "level": "h2",
            "anchor": "what-it-is"
          }
        },
        "content_6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A mandibular advancement device is an appliance you wear in your mouth while you sleep. It holds your lower jaw slightly forward.</p><p>Some oral appliances are recommended for certain adults after an evaluation by a professional. For sleep apnea, clinical guidelines prefer custom-made, adjustable appliances fitted and followed up by a dentist.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_7": {
          "type": "callout",
          "settings": {
            "style": "caution",
            "icon": "alert",
            "title": "Important",
            "text": "<p>An oral device doesn't replace a diagnosis or treatment from a healthcare provider. What studies show about some oral appliances doesn't prove that every appliance works.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_8": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What options are there",
            "level": "h2",
            "anchor": "options"
          }
        },
        "content_9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Some solutions act in the mouth, others in the nose, and some aren't products at all. The table below compares <strong>how they work</strong>, not which works best — that depends on each person.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
